        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): escalate Codex usage-limit prompt errors to model fallback",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen a Codex-backed turn hits the ChatGPT/Codex subscription usage limit,\nthe harness surfaces a classified `promptError` (not a thrown\n`FailoverError` at the turn boundary). The host prompt failover path then\nprefers auth-profile rotation for `rate_limit` before model fallback.\nAccount-scoped usage limits are not fixed by rotating profiles on the\nsame subscription, so configured cross-provider fallbacks (for example\nCodex primary + Anthropic fallback) never engage and the run ends\nterminally.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```console\n$ pnpm exec vitest run src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/failover-policy.test.ts\n✓ 42 tests passed (includes #103734 profileRotated escalation cases)\n\n$ node -e '...'  # Codex usage-limit classifier gate\nisCodexSubscriptionUsageLimit true\nplain rate limit false\n```\n\nWith `fallbackConfigured: true` and `profileRotated: true` (the host now\nsets this for Codex subscription usage-limit text),\n`resolveRunFailoverDecision` returns `fallback_model` instead of\n`rotate_profile`. Without configured fallbacks it still returns\n`surface_error` (no-fallback contract preserved; ClawSweeper guidance on\n#103868).\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** Codex usage-limit promptError blocks model fallback\n- **Real environment tested:** macOS worktree fix/codex-usage-limit-failover; unit + decision-table proof (no live Codex quota burn)\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:** vitest failover-policy tests; node regex gate for usage-limit detection\n- **Evidence after fix:** tests show `fallback_model` when fallbacks configured and rotation skipped; `surface_error` when not\n- **Observed result after fix:** Codex subscription usage-limit path is eligible for outer model fallback without removing the generic `fallbackConfigured` guard\n- **What was not tested:** live depleted Codex subscription with real multi-provider fallback (account-dependent)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Detect Codex subscription usage-limit prompt error text on the host\n- Skip auth-profile rotation for that case; keep generic rate-limit rotation\n- Preserve no-fallback `surface_error` when no model fallbacks are configured\n- Narrower than #103868 (no OAuth drive-by, no removal of fallbackConfigured)\n\nCloses #103734\n\nRelated: #103868 (closed; recommended preserving no-fallback contract), #95400 (embedded result classification)\n",
        "branch": "fix/codex-usage-limit-failover",
